  "result": "Perfect! All 93 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT calculation:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **New function in `src/invoices.js`:**\n   - **`lineVat(line)`** \u2014 Calculates VAT for a single line:\n     - Amount after discount = lineTotal - lineDiscount\n     - VAT = amountAfterDiscount \u00d7 (vatRate / 100)\n     - Rounded with roundCents() and clamped to 0\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()` in `src/invoices.js`:**\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - total = subtotal - discount + vat\n   - VAT is the sum of all individual line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText()` in `src/render.js`:**\n   - Shows \"Discount: -\u20ac...\" line if discount > 0\n   - Shows \"VAT: \u20ac...\" line if VAT > 0\n   - Both lines appear just before the \"Total: \u20ac...\" line\n   - All amounts formatted with formatEuros()\n\n4. **Tests added (11 VAT-specific tests):**\n   - lineVat calculation with various discount and VAT rate combinations\n   - VAT with zero discount, zero VAT rate, reduced VAT rate (9%)\n   - invoiceTotals with multiple VAT rates and VAT-exempt lines\n   - renderInvoiceText showing/hiding VAT line appropriately\n   - Discount and VAT lines together in proper order\n\nVAT is calculated per line on the discounted amount, then summed for the invoice total, which is properly rounded and clamped to 0 minimum.",
